        "en": "The book claims that frequent remembrance of al-Mani repels harm. A separate practice writes the name 161 times around a city or town wall in Venus's hour, claiming protection from adversity. It also tells a story of sages placing it on Mardin fortress, which no one could capture. One hundred and sixty-one is the writing count. The fortress story is the book's account, not evidence of guaranteed security."
